{"title":"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Steakmath_(simple_and_rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Steakmath (simple and rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2ebb0bbd7374a1aab711a7f0e4707b398113e8f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, define the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c1c1c657c50f64a117edc2dabca6dc5baa4ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1, a_2, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d5b948fd2e8a82be18042d192710914b5e819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e5005fa83196dcdb7e5270b0dc20e1f13e22bd4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{n+1} =  \\begin{cases} \\sqrt{a_n} &amp; \\text{if } \\sqrt{a_n} \\text{ is an integer,} \\\\ a_n + 3 &amp; \\text{otherwise.} \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"53\" />Determine all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5c7c921b3334f6ecf58c241eeea42acf0ce71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> such that there exists a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/0735b2456caf7357043e86f6b878eb75682fb4a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> for infinitely many values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First we observe the following:\n</p><p>When we start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70bfe1974b1232f2083af888265aa9f97e2d5b98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f24d5fd63474eae3b7a6519812f35f77fe7908a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/2365bcad6903f7116aa7186f16232e21d0cc61ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/841bbe5d577aef1d0936a0b31891f91728e82326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> and the pattern <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229ef03352b6afcd7e8343bc826c75616d1ff471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,6,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> repeats.\n</p><p>When we start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107416469b0acd8353315204dac517e9e46b806b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f09a54fcb485c6fa85ece0a567826fdfe98cb1c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffce335a846c1048a9d985eb07371ffc96eaf752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d6a6beca57ebb0620444f8c500cad19e42ce615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and the pattern <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229ef03352b6afcd7e8343bc826c75616d1ff471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,6,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> repeats.\n</p><p>When we start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d523ec68a690e1ca4453514ef442ec2678ce1e6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/383679febc17d3b8a4563f9010e3eea9caca402a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9febcc3c5c6270d534813fb398a7b04f67c47174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb28e68db841ecb13ecee0b59afb9cfd302b1362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> and the pattern <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229ef03352b6afcd7e8343bc826c75616d1ff471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,6,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> repeats.\n</p><p>When we start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/989fb10bfc248055a768bee681d0003bd8a8a70a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad5222a52d9cdeeb67cc0043fa466a71f3646cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c059cedecd2cd671309a7253222ce1f3549fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />,..., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/48697bf1f1585d9d3c348c94c596ea82b385c6b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_8=36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2ee40c3fef76cad744aaa8ddd8f71404bcc303a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_9=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c34f6bc10b34ac04d4749ffe03df710581555d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10}=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/b/50b773d53b1c7ebc644ec7c689918d95f92de947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{11}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> and the pattern <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229ef03352b6afcd7e8343bc826c75616d1ff471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,6,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> repeats.\n</p><p>When this pattern <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229ef03352b6afcd7e8343bc826c75616d1ff471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,6,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> repeats, this means that there exists a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/0735b2456caf7357043e86f6b878eb75682fb4a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> for infinitely many values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and that number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2be532734af658cb22bfd47e28a5f913b711206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>When we start with any number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b48c1dc2b893e51f3433b86c90d1a57731b402e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0\\not\\equiv 0\\; mod\\; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />, we don't see a repeating pattern.\n</p><p>Therefore the claim is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3ba376682517bada54b407d40ecc6b26b4d82b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=3k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer and we need to prove this claim.\n</p><p>When we start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3ba376682517bada54b407d40ecc6b26b4d82b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=3k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />, the next term if it is not a square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/7/5c7f416b1a45567f63024528cf1309ccef7c4518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3k+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe6c3a8e33d059a189a05ac7d9832aa9c0b459e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3k+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> and so on until we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d9161062fe5baebfe2414eba262b4ff61a57816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3k+3p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is an integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f559199cc09572cb3d8cca1659d8923968c32f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+p)=3q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"21\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is an integer.  Then the next term will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1c5956f6d436286e8f304f78e029be0198a836.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{9q^2}=3q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"24\" /> and the pattern repeats again when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c26c5d67f44183e9bc5805a044498ce69927704.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> or when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a99bb04a5525117c5f4322d6886c384021a05ecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>In order for these patterns to repeat, any square in the sequence need to be a multiple of 3.  \n</p><p>To try the other two cases where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b48c1dc2b893e51f3433b86c90d1a57731b402e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0\\not\\equiv 0\\; mod\\; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />, we can try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/1393a601b27df5ed63ec286a84fc9397f2006de5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=3k\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" /> then the next terms will be in the form  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/13952538d45eabc3991875407ad54226a97719d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3k+3p\\pm 1 = 3(k+p) \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd6142616662443e46be9b8a834ded8d7a9bf444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(k+p) \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> is a square, it will not be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd6142616662443e46be9b8a834ded8d7a9bf444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(k+p) \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> is not a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb661b9327905ed76e08be7ac2b5f6729526070.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(k+p) \\pm 1 \\ne 9q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"21\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df30d62d21b1447407d214eed0cba20536580119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(k+p) \\pm 1 \\equiv \\pm 1\\; mod\\; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88bb97ca2ab6cdd3823e982b86f796662e4a58c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /> would have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/544c666cd5c09063e7fdb1749d8c31fd1eaec9e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(k+p)}{3} \\pm \\frac{1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"40\" /> which is not an integer even if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/2/c0255f3e90bc4f4517c5a4d9be0d509bff512ce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore the pattern doesn't repeat for any of the other cases where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/1393a601b27df5ed63ec286a84fc9397f2006de5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=3k\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" /> and only repeats when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055d1c38aacffb56dc79260d1cfdde5cf8f1dca0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0\\equiv 0\\; mod\\; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>So, the answer to this problem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/896005a32cae858e4ade97e43523e4c242123469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=3k\\;\\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}^{+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cebd936059935f0111a3e5b36db40aabf79fcb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=3,6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b27278ca6484934a3d46e5234b780501922f617c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv b \\mod 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/a/57a1b2f4ce9220330ccc4996d1b885f94d05b60a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv_3 b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />. First note if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/2071af54a9d5d407b391b7dd1e522e3fe3d61c91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\equiv_3 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/7960214b43f8c75812c7caf2d8d57c8163b5fbd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+3k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> is never an integer squared because all integers squared are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We claim such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5c7c921b3334f6ecf58c241eeea42acf0ce71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />'s are precisely those divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. By induction:\n</p><p>Base cases: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a16f2d4ee29c282b705559743af4c40867c16c88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> we get the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f0591569ddaa237e78c24568b9f96ecf3270603e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,4,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> which diverges. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/a/f1ad32e9032890273ea370e8d09d2545aa158590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> we're done. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70bfe1974b1232f2083af888265aa9f97e2d5b98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> we get the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f32e832497257e4d8eeae3cb1c5bb9fa81869b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,6,9,3,...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> as desired. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087e5fe6736c73455d7a8e3265b5676b61ac3451.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0bad78c0b52d180bb51ac7f3f167374b4d38a73b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> and we're done. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b05b67c50bdf992fb1b83a4c1d310e87878e7295.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> we're done since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f2736e270bf25c9d947e7cb1fb1ebefe72efe5de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\equiv_3 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107416469b0acd8353315204dac517e9e46b806b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> we get the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/0/eb0be07cd66729a26a24d2ff419beb2aa19ac6bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6,9,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> which repeats.\n</p><p>Now suppose the induction holds for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888ef4a420b64d6cf555edd336cbf8930848e14f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1 \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/5/7156ec334a482032211b8ced8fbdab4cdd190d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv_3 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> we're done. Note if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48ce6d8cee7234c0f33b1bd9538dd830d1ec610a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-3=m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/89425212ff4d122173e1597322fed8ac633a015b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m+1)^2&gt;m^2+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"21\" /> sufficient <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c45a9440a903bd7c6cff6b0be3105608f3cd9e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />. i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8a927f498c3bf6f3be9889be85b5ef6e0eace1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />. We will need this.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/335363f18b2a6fcb3433e4e494eb235d52baf687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv_3 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />: \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer squared we're done by the induction hypothesis since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a0904d925689ea0a921cd1cef7ee9ec55ffdd7d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3|\\sqrt{n} &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"22\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/31503c8c86ff405ea9ae2dd6285eecb04550cb97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> isn't a perfect square we're done, since the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/9/329175231f14748d10fb9d8ca29c1a1d505f4ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 = n-3, a_1 =n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"17\" />, ... repeats by hypothesis. So write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48ce6d8cee7234c0f33b1bd9538dd830d1ec610a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-3=m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/67378f02b66997e8538f941ba5fca7e137e48bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3|m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" />. Then \n\\begin{align}\n(m+1)^2-m^2 &amp;\\equiv_3 1 \\\\\n(m+2)^2-m^2 &amp;\\equiv_3 1 \\\\\n(m+3)^2-m^2 &amp;\\equiv_3 0 \n\\end{align}\nso the sequence with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a6c434e16c12e9dc83d6b70e97bd789e1b07778.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> goes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65b69a18fa84ebb7f7459f04585efa00705a77de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,n+3,...,(m+3)^2,m+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/116a2ae5f298ee1c584414f797f4addb314b9ecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3|m+3&lt;n=m^2+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"21\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7cc262421ffff96a6fb5acd65c3437ee5e77127.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8a927f498c3bf6f3be9889be85b5ef6e0eace1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />) we're done by hypothesis.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/53334c9774c72782bfed13041f49e24764e7c182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\equiv_3 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />: \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer squared we're done by the induction hypothesis (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f5fd2c00f691df88f1ee10175b42d1694b1a6f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\nmid \\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"22\" />).  \nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/31503c8c86ff405ea9ae2dd6285eecb04550cb97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> isn't an integer squared we're done since the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e2de0bccaa3b7d3c297e81bc76f9cd930b0e936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=n-3,a_1=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"17\" /> doesn't repeat by hypothesis. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48ce6d8cee7234c0f33b1bd9538dd830d1ec610a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-3=m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3eba2faae0181ac5c306c72168114084c5b8eec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\nmid m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/602915cbb49ea5787ae067bc7c90e3a562fd812e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\equiv_3 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df6de3074a107fc004f4fc28455d3afbdda5532f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m+1)^2-m^2 \\equiv_3 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"21\" /> so the sequence goes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f03cf6aa47111620b471657af61677ab76622a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,n+3,...,(m+1)^2,m+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"21\" /> and we're done since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed794601d90656a9bebd3708d382a42e27a8b306.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\nmid m+1&lt;n=m^2+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed99c85dd00eb11d60bb8d0332530445cf25c5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d034b51294ef53e016b9d7fefd837a865e52d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />). If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65ac0a864d67ee36799ed7dc375f4e0374dbfea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\equiv_3 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> then \n\\begin{align}\n(m+1)^2-m^2 &amp;\\equiv_3 2 \\\\ \n(m+2)^2-m^2 &amp;\\equiv_3 0 \n\\end{align}\nso the sequence goes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99fe8e3944c44a8b9b7924d61c767194ed7d4110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,n+3,...,(m+2)^2,m+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"21\" /> and we're done by hypothesis since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/6/0069905c3f1cda0188d55003cc2d888235d69b79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\nmid m+2 &lt; n=m^2+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed99c85dd00eb11d60bb8d0332530445cf25c5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/83870118206bd0e612b5c9e3def2ef95460e368b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />). \n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Steakmath_.28simple_and_rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Steakmath_(simple_and_rigorous)\">Video Solution by Steakmath (simple and rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Steakmath (simple and rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5lqW6dDCZVA\">https://youtu.be/5lqW6dDCZVA</a>\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO\" title=\"2017 IMO\">2017 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003503\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.050 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.071 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 680/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1210/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22773/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.281      1 -total\n 54.25%    8.290      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 44.62%    6.818      1 Template:IMO_box\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15788:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003503 and revision id 280064. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}